generation.prompt:
A 10-site spin-1/2 chain is described by the TFIM H = -J * sum_{i=0}^{8} sigma^z_i sigma^z_{i+1} - h * sum_{i=0}^{9} sigma^x_i with J = 1 and open boundary conditions. Sweep h/J from 0.20 to 2.00 in steps of 0.05 (37 parameter points). Simulate the ground-state preparation under a realistic hardware noise model: two-qubit CNOT gates have a depolarizing error rate p_2q = 0.01, single-qubit gates have error p_1q = 0.005, and measurement readout has a 2% bit-flip error per qubit. At each h, measure: (1) m_z = (1/10) sum_i <sigma^z_i>, (2) chi_z = 10*(<m_z^2> - <m_z>^2), (3) Binder cumulant U4 = 1 - <m_z^4>/(3<m_z^2>^2), and (4) end-to-end correlation C(9) = <sigma^z_0 sigma^z_9>. Apply error mitigation in four configurations and compare: (a) raw noisy, (b) readout error mitigation only, (c) zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) only (using gate folding at 1x, 3x, 5x noise and Richardson extrapolation), and (d) both readout mitigation and ZNE combined. Use N_shots = 8192 per parameter point per noise configuration. Identify h_c from the chi_z peak in each configuration and report how mitigation shifts the estimate. Use 5000 shots for calibration matrix estimation. Report: estimated_critical_point (h_c for all four mitigation configurations), critical_point_error (|h_c - 1.0| for each configuration), observable_accuracy (mean absolute deviation of all observables from ideal noiseless simulation), phase_classification_accuracy (at noise level p_2q=0.01 with full mitigation), and noise_aware_performance (residual critical-point error after full mitigation vs. raw noisy estimate).

Task inputs:
{
  "physical_system": "1D transverse-field Ising model (TFIM), 10 sites, open boundary conditions, with two-qubit and readout noise and error mitigation",
  "num_spins": 10,
  "hamiltonian": {
    "expression": "H = -J * sum_{i=0}^{8} sigma^z_i sigma^z_{i+1} - h * sum_{i=0}^{9} sigma^x_i",
    "parameters": {
      "J": 1.0,
      "h": "swept"
    },
    "boundary_conditions": "open",
    "matrix_dimension": 1024
  },
  "parameter_sweep": {
    "parameter": "h/J",
    "values": "0.20, 0.25, 0.30, ..., 2.00",
    "num_points": 37,
    "step": 0.05
  },
  "observables_provided": [
    "longitudinal order parameter: m_z = (1/10) * sum_i <sigma^z_i>",
    "magnetic susceptibility: chi_z = 10 * Var[m_z] = 10 * (<m_z^2> - <m_z>^2)",
    "Binder cumulant: U4 = 1 - <m_z^4> / (3 * <m_z^2>^2)",
    "two-point correlation at maximum separation: C(9) = <sigma^z_0 sigma^z_9>"
  ],
  "noise_model": {
    "two_qubit_depolarizing": "p_2q = 0.01 applied to each CNOT gate",
    "single_qubit_depolarizing": "p_1q = 0.005 applied to each single-qubit gate",
    "readout_error": "epsilon = 0.02 (2% bit-flip per qubit per measurement shot, symmetric)"
  }
}

Required Python interface:
def solve_tfim_10site_obc_zne():
Return a dictionary with these outputs: estimated_critical_point, critical_point_error, observable_accuracy, phase_classification_accuracy, noise_aware_performance
Supported environment: Python 3.12; Qiskit 1.4.5, qiskit-aer 0.17.2, qiskit-algorithms 0.3.1, qiskit-optimization 0.6.1, PennyLane 0.45.1, NumPy, SciPy, NetworkX, dimod and neal (dwave-neal). Use qiskit_aer for Aer, qiskit_algorithms for algorithms, and QuantumCircuit.assign_parameters for parameter binding. qiskit.Aer, BasicAer, execute, aqua, and bind_parameters are unavailable. 
Include imports and helper functions. Do not execute at import time. Put scientific explanations in code comments/docstrings. Return only Python code.

